Short:        Preformatted CopperNova CNP2 emulator demo
Author:       Ilkka Lehtoranta
Uploader:     ilkleht@gmail.com (Ilkka Lehtoranta)
Type:         disk/misc
Version:      1.0-preview.7
Requires:     AmigaOS 2.04, 68000 or newer, TD64-capable hardfile driver
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 2.04

This optional emulator demo contains BlankCNP2.rdb.gz, this README and
the license notices for the embedded handler.
For installation on your own partition, use the handler and formatter in
CopperNova.lha.

Decompress BlankCNP2.rdb.gz on the host. The resulting image is slightly
over 4.06 GiB. Attach it as a second, writable RDB hardfile and boot from
your usual system disk. A copy of the preview handler is already installed
in the image's RDB. The preformatted, nonbootable CNP2 v6 partition CNP0: is
4 GiB + 64 MiB and uses DOS type 0x434E5032 (CNP2).

Keep a separate copy of the original image if you want to start over.
This image is intended for emulators. Writing it to a physical disk
overwrites that disk's partition table and volume contents.

CopperNova is MIT-licensed. The source and license are available at
https://github.com/ilehtoranta/CopperFS
